Package: dsfit
Title: Fit and Compare Detection Functions for Line-Transect Survey Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Camille", "Ross", email = "camille.ross@maine.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1428-2294"))
Description: Fits a set of candidate detection functions to line-transect
    distance data and compares them on the quantities that matter for
    abundance, not on AIC alone. Models are fitted through 'mrds' so that every
    candidate comes off the same likelihood machinery and the gamma key function
    is available alongside half-normal, hazard-rate and uniform. Enforces the
    conditions under which a comparison is meaningful: truncation must be held
    constant within a model set, and binned and exact distances cannot be ranked
    together. Reports effective strip half-width and its coefficient of
    variation next to each fit, since two models within two AIC of one another
    can imply materially different abundance. Takes the flatfile produced by
    'distsamp' or any equivalent table.
